        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hume Auctioneers - We Get The Pick Of The Crop.\n\nPerhaps Monasterevin's most exclusive address, Drogheda Street was designed by the Earls of Drogheda in the 19th century and is home to some of the finest homes in all of County Kildare. A leafy enclave where a beautiful mix of period homes, schools and a magnificent church all combine to create a street of unrivalled beauty. At the bottom of Drogheda street is the beautiful Grand Canal with the train station just beside it.\n\nThe Chestnuts is a beautiful 4 bay Victorian residence beautifully set at the quiet end of the street.\n\nStep inside the attractive entrance and through the impressive vestibule hallway to a property which is rich in character and showcases an exceptional collection of beautifully preserved period details. \n\nA welcoming entrance hall immediately sets the tone, with its warm parquet flooring, decorative cornicing and elegant staircase featuring turned spindles, a polished timber handrail and exquisite carved detailing.\n\nThe generously proportioned living room is filled with natural light from twin windows and retains all the grandeur expected of a fine period residence. High ceilings, deep cornicing, an ornate ceiling rose and a handsome cast-iron fireplace with inset stove create a wonderfully elegant setting. Double doors lead to the Kitchen dining room.\n\nThe spacious kitchen/breakfast room combines traditional character with excellent everyday practicality, featuring extensive bespoke cabinetry, a range-style cooker, tiled flooring, exposed ceiling beams and ample room for family dining.\n\nTo the rear, a charming south-facing sunroom with a glazed roof provides a bright and relaxing additional living space. \n\nThe ground-floor accommodation is completed by a useful utility room and guest WC.\n\n Throughout, the impressive ceiling heights, fine joinery, original-style windows with working shutters, wall panelling and intricate plasterwork give the interior a rare sense of craftsmanship, warmth and timeless distinction.\n\nThe exceptional scale and period character continue to the first floor, where a gracious split-level landing is beautifully illuminated by a striking arched stained-glass window. High ceilings, elegant cornicing, a traditional spindle balustrade, polished timber handrail and chandelier create an impressive sense of arrival.\n\nThere are three outstanding double bedrooms, each offering superb proportions, high ceilings and abundant natural light. Two bedrooms benefit from private shower en suites. The layout and size of the landing and bedroom three is such that with minimum outlay this room could easily convert to 2 large singles.\n\n\nA spacious family bathroom completes the accommodation, fitted with a full-sized bath, pedestal wash-hand basin and WC. \n\nThroughout the first floor, deep skirting boards, substantial door surrounds, attractive window detailing and beautifully proportioned rooms preserve the elegance and distinction of this fine period home.\n\nTo the rear is a charming and exceptionally private courtyard garden, finished with attractive paving. An original brick wall provides a wonderful period backdrop, while a useful pedestrian entrance offers convenient access for bins and deliveries without passing through the house.\n\nSchools, shops, Church and Train Station are all on your doorstep at The Chestnuts.\n\nMonasterevin offers an exceptional quality of life, combining the charm of a welcoming country town with superb transport connections and an excellent range of local amenities. The picturesque River Barrow and the Barrow Blueway provide wonderful opportunities for walking, cycling, fishing and enjoying the outdoors, while the town?s excellent children?s playground is a major attraction for families. Monasterevin also benefits from a mainline train station, placing Dublin and surrounding towns within easy commuting distance, while access to the M7 motorway is just five minutes away. The renowned Kildare Village shopping destination and the National Stud and Japanese Gardens are approximately ten minutes by car.\n\nThe town is particularly well served by two brand new primary and secondary schools both within walking distance of The Chestnuts, as are churches, shops, cafés and essential everyday services. A strong sporting tradition is supported by a wide selection of clubs and facilities, including GAA, soccer, rugby, athletics and water-based activities. With its beautiful riverside setting, vibrant community spirit and outstanding accessibility, Monasterevin is an increasingly sought-after location for families, commuters and anyone seeking the perfect balance between town and country living.\n\nThe Barrow Blueway is a scenic, predominantly off-road walking, running and cycling route following the Barrow Line of the Grand Canal, passing through Rathangan, Monasterevin and Vicarstown. The Monasterevin section is particularly picturesque, incorporating the historic canal harbour, old bridges, locks, peaceful countryside and the remarkable aqueduct where the canal crosses above the River Barrow. It provides an excellent year-round amenity for leisurely walking, running and cycling\n\nViewing of this exceptional home is highly recommended.\n"
